{# ONE PAGER, FOR EVERY LIST THAT PAGES RATHER THAN SCROLLS.

   A CARD IS BOUNDED BY ITS PAGE SIZE, not by a scrollbar inside it: the count
   on the left, the pages on the right, and the window between them. Every
   page number is a link, so where you are in a list is in the address.

   ONE IDIOM, AND THE LIST'S ORDER PICKS THE WORDS. A list ordered by TIME
   pages backwards through it, so its ends are "newer" and "older"; a list
   ordered by a name or a number has no such ends and pages "previous" and
   "next". The words follow the ORDER and never the page, so one list that
   can be reordered says both at different times, and two lists in the same
   order always say the same.

   TWO WAYS TO ADDRESS A PAGE, because a page may hold two lists. A list that
   owns the address hands over its `query` and the links are the route's own
   parameters; a second list on the same page hands over `base`, its own
   `param` and whatever else it must carry, so two searches and two pagers on
   one card stack cannot filter each other.

   IT SAYS WHEN IT IS FILTERED. "5 of 12 stations · filtered from 30" is two
   different facts about one list, and a reader who cannot see the second one
   reads the first as the whole. #}
{% set byTime = byTime ?? false %}
{% set back = byTime ? '&larr; Newer' : '&larr; Previous' %}
{% set on = byTime ? 'Older &rarr;' : 'Next &rarr;' %}
{% set extra = extra ?? '' %}
{# Every page's address, built once, so the markup below is the design and
   nothing else. #}
{% set urls = range(1, max(1, pages))|map(number => query is defined
    ? path(app.request.attributes.get('_route'), app.request.attributes.get('_route_params')|merge(query.with('page', number ~ '')))
    : base ~ '?' ~ param ~ '=' ~ number ~ extra) %}
{% if pages > 1 or (scope is defined and scope > total) %}
    <div class="pgr">
        <span class="cnt">
            {%- if total %}{{ from }}&ndash;{{ to }}{% else %}0{% endif %} of {{ total }} {{ noun }}
            {%- if scope is defined and scope > total %} &middot; filtered from {{ scope }}{% endif -%}
        </span>
        <span class="sp"></span>
        {% if pages > 1 %}
            <a class="{{ page == 1 ? 'off' : '' }}" href="{{ urls[max(1, page - 1) - 1] }}">{{ back|raw }}</a>
            {% for number in 1..pages %}
                {% if number == page %}
                    <span class="pg-n on">{{ number }}</span>
                {% else %}
                    <a href="{{ urls[number - 1] }}">{{ number }}</a>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
            <a class="{{ page == pages ? 'off' : '' }}" href="{{ urls[min(pages, page + 1) - 1] }}">{{ on|raw }}</a>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
